# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 1 of the Tutorial

[B11's Example 5.7]

e,1,0,36
r1,1,2,1'k
r2,2,3,3'k
r3,3,0,2'k

analysis: dc
note: The first simulation in the tutorial. The Evaluate line checks the power balance: the resistors consume exactly what the source delivers, so the four powers come to zero.
rounding: 3
si: yes
units: yes
evaluate: pr1 + pr2 + pr3 + pe


[HK5's Figure 1-26]

e1,1,0,120
r1,1,2,30
e2,2,3,30
r2,3,0,15

analysis: dc
note: The 30 V source consumes 60 W rather than delivering it, which is why -pe2 comes out negative.
rounding: 3
si: yes
units: yes
evaluate: pr1 + pr2 + pe1 + pe2


